OL,3,GNEWSATributes to 'much loved' cyclist
OL,4,Akilled in Port Glasgow crash
OL,5,
OL,6,FTributes have been paid to a "much
OL,7,Floved" cyclist who died in a crash on a
OL,8,Fbusy Inverclyde road while taking part
OL,9,Fin a training session with fellow
OL,10,Friders.
OL,12,FIain McTavish, 46, was one of three
OL,13,Fcyclists in a collision with a blue
OL,14,FFord C-Max Zetec on the A8 in Port
OL,15,FGlasgow shortly after 19:00 on Tuesday.
OL,16,FHe died at the scene.
OL,18,FTwo other male cyclists, aged 37 and
OL,19,F27, were taken to hospital following
OL,20,Fthe crash on the road's westbound
OL,21,Fcarriageway between the Langbank and
OL,22,FWoodhall roundabouts.
OL,23,APub: 08-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
FL,428,420,260,160,0,100
